title: Veeam: Scale-out repository
agents: special
catalog: os/storage
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors a scale-out backup repository of a Veeam Backup &
 Replication server, collected via the Veeam special agent. It reports the
 number of configured performance extents and their statuses, the
 description, whether the capacity tier and archive tier are configured
 and enabled, and the placement policy.

 This check does not report capacity. A scale-out repository has no
 capacity of its own; capacity lives on its extents, which appear as
 separate {Backup repository} services.

 Each performance extent can report zero or more statuses at the same
 time. {Normal}, {Pending} and {Sealed} are {OK} by default. {Evacuate},
 {Maintenance}, {ResyncRequired} and {TenantEvacuating} are {WARN} by
 default. Every status is individually configurable. An unrecognised
 status makes the extent {UNKNOWN}. The service state is the worst state
 of all its extents.

 A scale-out repository with no performance extents configured is {WARN}
 by default; this is also configurable.

discovery:
 One service is created for each scale-out repository reported by the API.

item:
 The name of the scale-out repository.
